<Layout
  title="Kirsten King, MSW"
  description="Kirsten King, MSW — Fundraising & Communications Director, co-founder of Blessed Are They."
  active="about"
>
  <FounderProfile
    name="Kirsten King, MSW"
    role="Fundraising & Communications Director · Co-founder"
    photo="/uploads/ChatGPT Image Aug 24, 2026, 05_54_31 PM.png"
    objectPosition="50% 25%"
    bioHtml={[
      `She is a wife, mother of four, a creative that knows no bounds, and a fearless follower of the Holy Spirit who believes that some of the best work God does begins with a simple, <b><i>&ldquo;Yes, Lord. I'm in.&rdquo;</i></b>`,
      `With decades of experience in parish life, ministry, evangelization, faith formation, international missionary work, fundraising, marketing, and creative development, Kirsten has learned that the Lord rarely wastes a season. He uses each one to shape us, prune us, and reveal new ways for our gifts to bear fruit.`,
      `When Kirsten was young and newly married, her ministry looked like a battlefield. She spent years in the trenches of youth ministry — walking alongside teenagers, serving families, building programs, and learning firsthand the joys and challenges of leading others toward Christ.`,
      `Then life changed. Her family grew, her vocation as a wife and mother deepened, and the Lord began to prune some of the ways she had always used her gifts. What once required her to be everywhere began to look different. She discovered that ministry could also happen through a kitchen table, a conversation in the car, a creative idea born after bedtime, or simply being present to the people God had entrusted to her. She began finding new ways to use her gifts that honored both her calling to ministry and her first vocation as a wife and mother.`,
      `Relocating to Tennessee in 2022 opened yet another chapter. <b><i>Rather than trying to fit her vocation into her work, she began building her work around her vocation.</i></b>`,
      `Through every season, one thread has remained: <strong><i>capturing the story.</i></strong> Kirsten has a passion for seeing what God is doing beneath the surface and helping others recognize it, too.`,
      `Today, her greatest mission field is still the home. She is passionate about building up the domestic church and equipping parents to be the primary witnesses of faith, truth, love, and human dignity to their children. She believes that some of the most beautiful work of the Church happens quietly — in ordinary homes, around ordinary tables, in the messy and sacred reality of everyday life.`,
      `And perhaps more than anything, Kirsten has learned that <strong>there is grace for every season.</strong> The battlefield, the pruning, the rebuilding, the unexpected turns — they are all part of the story. And the story is always worth capturing.`,
    ]}
    focusHtml="<b><i>Her focus in Program Development:</i></b><br />Crafting the connections and conversations for parents and children with practical applications to daily life, with real, focused and impactful intention."
  />
</Layout>
